<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 27 August, from 479 BCE to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">479 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greeks defeat the Persian army at Plataea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Greek alliance led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> defeated the Persian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a>, on a date traditionally placed in late August. The victory ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>'s invasion of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 CE <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British forces defeat Washington at the Battle of Long Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General William Howe outflanked and routed the Continental Army in Brooklyn, the largest battle of the war. Two nights later Washington's army escaped across the East River.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1859 CE <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edwin Drake strikes oil in Pennsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Drilling near Titusville, Edwin Drake's well struck oil at about 21 metres. It was the first commercially successful oil well in the US and launched the modern petroleum industry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1928 CE <span class="tih-ago">98 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fifteen nations sign the Kellogg-Briand Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signatories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> renounced war as an instrument of national policy. The pact had no means of enforcement, but it later underpinned charges of crimes against peace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1939 CE <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Heinkel He 178 makes the first jet-powered flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Test pilot Erich Warsitz flew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinkel">Heinkel</a> He 178 at Rostock-Marienehe, the first flight of an aircraft powered by a turbojet. Days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
